.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_CTX
holds data about multiple decoders, as needed to figure out what the
input data is and to attempt to unpack it into one of several possible
related results.
This also includes chaining decoders, so the output from one can become
the input for another.
This allows having generic format decoders such as PEM to DER, as well
as more specialized decoders like DER to RSA.
.Pp
The chains may be limited by specifying an input type, which is
considered a starting point.
This is both considered by
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_add_extra ,
which will stop adding one more decoder implementations when it has
already added those that take the specified input type, and functions
like
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_from_bio 3 ,
which will only start the decoding process with the decoder
implementations that take that input type.
For example, if the input type is set to
.Qo Li DER Qc ,
a PEM to DER decoder will be ignored.
.Pp
The input type can also be NULL, which means that the caller doesn't
know what type of input they have.
In this case,
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_from_bio 3
will simply try with one decoder implementation after the other, and
thereby discover what kind of input the caller gave it.
.Pp
For every decoding done, even an intermediary one, a constructor
provided by the caller is called to attempt to construct an appropriate
type / structure that the caller knows how to handle from the current
decoding result.
The constructor is set with
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct .
.Pp
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE
is an opaque structure that contains data about the decoder that was
just used, and that may be useful for the constructor.
There are some functions to extract data from this type, described
further down.
.Ss Functions
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_new
creates a new empty
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_CTX .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_settable_ctx_params
returns an
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array of parameter descriptors.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_params
attempts to set parameters specified with an
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array
.Em params .
These parameters are passed to all decoders that have been added to the
.Fa ctx
so far.
Parameters that an implementation doesn't recognise should be ignored by
it.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_free
frees the given context
.Fa ctx .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_add_decoder
populates the
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_CTX
.Fa ctx
with a decoder, to be used to attempt to decode some encoded input.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_add_extra
finds decoders that generate input for already added decoders, and adds
them as well.
This is used to build decoder chains.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_input_type
sets the starting input type.
This limits the decoder chains to be considered, as explained in the
general description above.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_input_structure
sets the name of the structure that the input is expected to have.
This may be used to determines what decoder implementations may be used.
NULL is a valid input structure, when it's not relevant, or when the
decoder implementations are expected to figure it out.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_num_decoders
gets the number of decoders currently added to the context
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct
sets the constructor
.Fa construct .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct_data
sets the constructor data that is passed to the constructor every time
it's called.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_cleanup
sets the constructor data
.Fa cleanup
function.
This is called by
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_CTX_free 3 .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_construct ,
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_construct_data
and
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_cleanup
return the values that have been set by
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct ,
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct_data
and
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_cleanup
respectively.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_export
is a fallback function for constructors that cannot use the data they
get directly for diverse reasons.
It takes the same decode instance
.Fa decoder_inst
that the constructor got and an object
.Fa reference ,
unpacks the object which it refers to, and exports it by creating an
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array that it then passes to
.Fa export_cb ,
along with
.Em export_arg .
.Ss Constructor
A
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_CONSTRUCT
gets the following arguments:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fa decoder_inst
The
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE
for the decoder from which the constructor gets its data.
.It Fa object
A provider-native object abstraction produced by the decoder.
Further information on the provider-native object abstraction can be
found in
.Xr provider-object 7 .
.It Fa construct_data
The pointer that was set with
.Xr OSSL_DECODE_CTX_set_construct_data 3 .
.El
.Pp
The constructor is expected to return 1 when the data it receives can be
constructed, otherwise 0.
.Pp
These utility functions may be used by a constructor:
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE_get_decoder
can be used to get the decoder implementation from a decoder instance
.Fa decoder_inst .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE_get_decoder_ctx
can be used to get the decoder implementation's provider context from a
decoder instance
.Fa decoder_inst .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE_get_input_type
can be used to get the decoder implementation's input type from a
decoder instance
.Fa decoder_inst .
.Pp
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE_get_input_structure 3
can be used to get the input structure for the decoder implementation
from a decoder instance
.Fa decoder_inst .
This may be NULL.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_new
returns a pointer to a
.Vt OSSL_DECODER_CTX ,
or NULL if the context structure couldn't be allocated.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_settable_ctx_params
returns an
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array, or NULL if none is available.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_params
returns 1 if all recognised parameters were valid, or 0 if one of them
was invalid or caused some other failure in the implementation.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_add_decoder ,
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_add_extra ,
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct ,
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_construct_data
and
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_set_cleanup
return 1 on success, or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_construct ,
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_construct_data
and
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_CTX_get_cleanup
return the current pointers to the constructor, the constructor data and
the cleanup functions, respectively.
.Pp
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_CTX_num_decoders 3
returns the current number of decoders.
It returns 0 if
.Fa ctx
is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_DECODER_export
returns 1 on success, or 0 on failure.
.Pp
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE_decoder 3
returns an
.Vt OSSL_DECODER
pointer on success, or NULL on failure.
.Pp
.Xr OSSL_DECODER_INSTANCE_decoder_ctx 3
returns a provider context pointer on success, or NULL on failure.
